WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.040
For months now, it's been nothing but hype
for Avengers: Endgame.

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:08.490
But some fans' steady enthusiasm took a slight
dip in the days leading up to the theatrical

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:12.190
launch of the superhero epic, when they learned
that Endgame would go against the Marvel movie

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:14.340
grain and not feature a post-credits scene.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:18.620
We're treading into spoiler territory, both
for the experience of watching Avengers: Endgame

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:20.740
on the big screen and for the movie itself.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:24.580
If you haven't yet seen the film and want
to walk in without knowing a single thing,

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:25.940
turn your attention away now.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:26.880
Last warning!

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.360
Many who saw the film in early screenings
got a bit up in arms over the lack of an end-credits

00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:35.600
stinger, but as it turns out, there are a
few very intriguing reasons why it's still

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.840
worth staying in your seat to watch the Endgame
credits the whole way through.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.040
After the beautiful closing shot of Endgame
fades to black, the credits start to roll.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:47.239
Important names like Joe and Anthony Russo,
the directors of Infinity War and Endgame,

00:00:47.239 --> 00:00:51.100
and Kevin Feige, the president of Marvel Studios
who has produced all of the films in the Marvel

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:53.240
Cinematic Universe, pop up on screen.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:57.360
Then, where a mid-credits scene would normally
fit, there's a gorgeous tribute to the principal

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:58.820
cast and guest stars of Endgame.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:03.120
Everyone you know and love is featured, except
for the six main Avengers, who get their own

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.129
special tribute.

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:08.759
Iron Man actor Robert Downey Jr., Captain
America star Chris Evans, Thor actor Chris

00:01:08.759 --> 00:01:13.310
Hemsworth, Bruce Banner/Hulk star Mark Ruffalo,
Black Widow actress Scarlett Johansson, and

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:16.940
Hawkeye actor Jeremy Renner each get heartwarming
video tributes featuring breathtaking new

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:17.940
artwork.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.320
The stars' signatures swipe across the screen,
making for an homage both well-deserved and

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:26.369
quite emotional, particularly considering
the events of Avengers: Endgame that viewers

00:01:26.369 --> 00:01:27.700
witnessed just before.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:28.780
But that's not all!

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:32.240
The credits don't entirely resume to business
as usual from there on.

00:01:32.249 --> 00:01:35.719
We advise audiences keep their butts in their
seats until the lights come on, lest they

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:39.400
miss an expertly placed MCU Easter egg at
the tail end of the credits.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:43.999
Right when it seems no other moviemaking details
will scroll on screen, keep your ears open.

00:01:43.999 --> 00:01:47.860
Immediately after the Marvel logo appears,
where a true post-credits scene would traditionally

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:50.540
be placed, a familiar sound rings out...

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:01.040
It may seem inconsequential to some, but for
die-hard Marvel fans, this sound effect means

00:02:01.049 --> 00:02:02.109
a great deal.

00:02:02.109 --> 00:02:06.049
Tony making an enormous sacrifice for the
greater good in Avengers: Endgame, something

00:02:06.049 --> 00:02:10.100
that the genius-billionaire-playboy-philanthropist
likely would have never done in his earlier

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:14.450
years, means the MCU as viewers have known
it thus far ends with Iron Man as well.

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:18.010
The split-second sound lets Iron Man be the
stopping point just as he was the starting

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:19.380
one all those years ago.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:23.200
Though it may not be a full-on post-credits
scene as Marvelites are used to seeing, it's

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:26.140
arguably more poignant than those sequences
have ever been.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:30.599
With Avengers: Endgame forgoing a post-credits
scene, the MCU is sailing ahead without any

00:02:30.599 --> 00:02:32.349
dangling threads trailing behind it.

00:02:32.349 --> 00:02:36.450
The franchise isn't ready to begin its fourth
phase just yet, as Feige has stated that it's

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:40.069
actually the Spidey sequel Spider-Man: Far
From Home that marks the end of the third

00:02:40.069 --> 00:02:43.579
phase, so there is technically one future
in-phase film to tease.

00:02:43.579 --> 00:02:47.799
However, Endgame is the coming-together of
the MCU's 11-year saga, and it would feel

00:02:47.799 --> 00:02:52.140
incredibly silly to tack on a sequence setting
up Spider-Man's next adventure: one, because

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:56.280
he wasn't in the movie until the final act,
and two, because a Spidey-centered tease would

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:59.460
be pretty jarring to see after the emotional
rollercoaster that was Endgame.

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:03.620
Marvel will leave the Phase 4-teasing up to
Far From Home when that film swings into theaters

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:06.060
this July, and everyone is better for it.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:10.459
Before then, though, re-watch Endgame as many
times as your heart desires, and be on alert

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:13.300
for the small but significant sound at the
end of the credits.

